## 6. CRITICAL CONSISTENCY CHECKS

Before issuing the final verdict, independently cross-check the blueprint for contradictions.

At minimum verify:

1. Every state referenced by an RPC is declared or explicitly identified as a proposed separate state.
2. Every foreign-key target exists in the proposed dependency sequence.
3. Every RLS policy references actual columns and compatible relationships.
4. Every RPC has a defined authorization boundary.
5. Every stock mutation has a matching allocation or movement effect.
6. No physical unit can be counted as both sellable and quarantined.
7. Reserved quantities cannot exceed eligible stock.
8. Courier custody is not confused with pharmacy shelf stock.
9. Settlement cannot commit without all required inventory and order mutations.
10. Cancellation cannot release stock after successful delivery settlement.
11. Return inspection cannot restore sellable stock twice.
12. An idempotency record cannot become permanently inconsistent with the business transaction.
13. Dispatch offers cannot produce multiple authoritative winning pharmacies for one request.
14. Candidate discovery cannot expose full address or phone information.
15. SECURITY DEFINER functions do not silently grant broad access.
16. The first-admin bootstrap does not create a public self-elevation path.
17. The sole-admin invariant is protected against concurrent multi-row mutations.
18. Delivery OTP removal does not remove account-login OTP.
19. Unresolved policies remain explicitly unresolved.
20. Existing local source facts are not presented as evidence of live Supabase state.

If any check fails, correct the blueprint or mark the relevant item BLOCKED. Do not conceal contradictions to obtain a positive verdict.

